From dac8ed6a9a657d170c95d3cbf967d5eae7fc551b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:35:27 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Hunter: Hunters' Rumours state, rare parts, turn-in, whistle

Hunters' Rumours (wiki) without the guild hunters' dialogues yet: per-hunter
rumours in server varps, assignment rules (each hunter's list, level, no
duplicate across hunters), the rare-part roll on catches with the wiki's
rates and pity thresholds (held part blocks, full inventory drops a rolled
part and destroys a pity part), turn-in XP ((level + 5) * 50/55/60) and the
tier's loot sack, and the quetzal whistle's Rumour op. Only creatures this
server can catch are assigned (wagtail, grey and carnivorous chinchompas,
herbiboar). ::rumour assigns, shows and hands in for testing.
